      "final_text": "Everything checks out. Here's a summary of what I built and verified:\n\n**Tool**: `tools/minidiff.py` \u2014 a dependency-free Python 3 CLI (stdlib `difflib` only) that:\n- Reads `argv[1]` and `argv[2]` as text files, splits each into whitespace-delimited words\n- Runs `difflib.unified_diff` at word granularity with `n=1` (1 word of context per hunk)\n- Prints only the changed hunks in unified-diff format when differences exist, exits `1`\n- Prints nothing and exits `0` when files are word-identical\n- Exits `2` with a usage message if not given exactly two file arguments\n\n**Fixtures**: `a.txt` and `b.txt`, each 5 lines of lighthouse prose, differing by exactly 3 single-word substitutions: `stormy`\u2192`calm`, `harbor.`\u2192`port.`, `flame.`\u2192`fire.`.\n\n**Verification performed**:\n- Ran the tool on `a.txt`/`b.txt`: produced clean hunk output, exit code `1`, empty stderr, all 3 substituted words (`stormy`/`calm`, `harbor`/`port`, `flame`/`fire`) present in the diff.\n- Ran the tool on `a.txt`/`a.txt` (identical): no output, exit code `0`.\n- Ran with missing args: correct usage message on stderr-equivalent, exit code `2`.\n- Confirmed the script parses with no syntax errors.\n\nNo bugs were found requiring a fix \u2014 the tool worked correctly on the first pass.\n\nFinal diff output between the two fixtures (exit code 1):\n\n```\n--- a.txt\n+++ b.txt\n@@ -6,3 +6,3 @@\n the\n-stormy\n+calm\n sky.\n@@ -25,3 +25,3 @@\n safe\n-harbor.\n+port.\n Waves\n@@ -46,2 +46,2 @@\n the\n-flame.\n+fire.\n```"
